Package: fathom
Title: See What is in a JSON Document Before You Parse It
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person("psychometrician", email = "psychometrician@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: One small vocabulary for seeing what is in a JSON document and
    getting a table out of it, spelled the same way in R and in Python. You
    point it at a document you have never seen and it reports whether the file
    is sound, what shapes it holds, and what one row could be, with every
    candidate priced. Output is proportional to the structure rather than to
    the data, so a 912 MB file and a 12 KB file produce descriptions of similar
    size. The package is a thin wrapper around the 'fathom' engine, which it
    invokes as a subprocess; the engine is compiled and bundled at install
    time, so an installed copy is self-contained and needs nothing else.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
URL: https://github.com/psychometrician/fathom,
    https://psychometrician.github.io/fathom-book/
BugReports: https://github.com/psychometrician/fathom/issues
